    "content": "All 19 checklist items have been tested and recorded.\n\n**Summary: 14 PASS / 5 FAIL**\n\nThe core job board flows work well — browsing, detail pages, search, filtering, application submission, dashboard counts, and confirmed deletion all behaved as expected.\n\n**Failures found:**\n\n1. **FT-18 — No edit capability.** There is no UI or route anywhere to edit a published job; dashboard rows offer only \"view applications\" and \"delete\".\n2. **CS-10 — Salary range not validated.** A job with minimum 150,000 and maximum 90,000 published successfully and displays the inverted range \"$150k - $90k\". (Required-field validation itself works.)\n3. **CS-11 — Duplicate applications allowed.** The same email could apply twice to the same job, creating two records with no error.\n4. **IX-19 — No persistence.** All state is in-memory; reloading restored seed data, discarding both new jobs and all submitted applications, and resurrecting the deleted job.\n5. **CT-20 — Off-by-one dates.** Items created seconds earlier display as \"Yesterday\" instead of today's date (2026-08-27).\n\nOne additional minor issue noted under FT-1 (not itself a failure): annual salary values entered for a **Contract** job are rendered with an \"/hr\" suffix (`$95000 - $135000/hr`), even though the form explicitly asks for an annual figure."
